The tree is frozen on 25.12.3 for this release of Raye. Moving to a newer
Dolphin means a merge: every file we touched is listed, with the reason,
in raye-changes/FX-<n>.txt (one file per work package). Read those first,
replay them on the new tree, then run the tests.


Changes kept from Ubuntu's dolphin packaging
--------------------------------------------

Ubuntu's source package 4:25.12.3-0ubuntu1 carries one patch. We keep it,
applied in the tree instead of in debian/patches, because we build native:

  require-baloo-widgets.patch
      Baloo Widgets is released with the minor version of the release
      service (25.12.0), so find_package(KF6BalooWidgets 25.12.3) never
      matches. The version asked for is now 25.12.0 and the package is
      REQUIRED: the file information panel is not optional for us.

Nothing else from Ubuntu's debian/ applies: the rest is packaging, and
ours is written from scratch in debian/.


What we do not build
--------------------

libdolphinvcs is Dolphin's public plugin interface. We do not build or
install our own copy: the package build-depends on libdolphinvcs-dev and
links the system libdolphinvcs6 (same 25.12.3 ABI), so dolphin-plugins
keeps loading into Files. If a future Dolphin changes that interface, the
system library has to move with us.

Qt private API
--------------

Like Dolphin, Files uses Qt private headers (qt6-base-private-dev), so the
package depends on qt6-base-private-abi of the Qt it was built with. Every
Qt update in the archive needs a rebuild of raye-files.
